window.EF_CRUX_DOC_PAGES=["ARAB & TURK INVASIONS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. First Muslim Invader — Group vs Individual\n●First Muslim invaders (group) = Arabs\n●First Arab/Muslim invader (individual) = Muhammad bin Qasim (712 CE) → Raja Dahir(Sindh) ko Battle of Rewar\nmein haraya\n TRICK — \"Group vs Individual\" trick\n💡\nSawaal ka wording dhyan se padho: \"Kaun the\" (group) → Arabs. \"Kaun tha\" (specific naam) → Muhammad bin\nQasim. Ek hi fact, do tarah se poocha jaata hai — wording decide karti hai answer ka format.\n2. Mahmud Ghazni vs Muhammad Ghori — Objective Ka Farak\n●Mahmud Ghazni → sirf LOOT/Wealth Plunder, permanent rule NAHI chahiye tha\n●Muhammad Ghori → PERMANENT RULE chahiye tha → Delhi Sultanate ki neenv\n TRICK — \"Ghazni=Khazana, Ghori=Ghar\" trick\n💡\nGhazni = \"Khazana\" (khazana/treasure loot karna, naam mein hi \"khaz\" jaisa sound) — sirf paisa leke wapas. Ghori =\n\"Ghar banaya\" (permanent ghar/rule sthapit kiya) — dono naam \"Gh\" se shuru hote hain isliye confuse hota hai, par\nkaam bilkul alag: ek ne khazana liya, doosre ne ghar basaya.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahmud Ghazni ka maksad = sirf wealth loot (permanent rule NAHI). Muhammad Ghori ka maksad = permanent rule.\nDono ka intention bilkul alag tha.\n3. Mahmud Ghazni — 17 Invasions, Somnath 16th\n●Total 17 invasions (1000-1027 CE) · 1st invasion(1001CE) → Jaipal(Hindu Shahi) ko haraya\n●16th invasion(1025-26CE) = Somnath Temple → Bhim I ko haraya, mandir loota\n TRICK — \"16≠17\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log Somnath ko 17th samajhte hain (kyunki total 17 hain, so lagta hai last wali hogi) — GALAT,\nSomnath 16th thi, ek aur invasion baad mein bhi hui. Yaad rakho: \"Somnath = Solah (16)\" — dono mein \"so\" sound\nmatch hota hai, isse seedha 16 yaad rahega.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSomnath Temple attack = 16th invasion (1025-26 CE), NA ki 17th — total 17 invasions the, par Somnath specifically\n16th thi.\n4. Bhim I vs Bhim II — Do Alag Gujarat Raja\n●Bhim I → Somnath(1025-26CE) mein Mahmud Ghazni se HAARA\n●Bhim II → Gujarat/Patan(1178CE) mein Muhammad Ghori ko HARAYA (Ghori ki PEHLI HAAR)\n TRICK — \"I=Haara, II=Jeeta\" trick\n💡\nBhim I (chota number, purana, ~1025) = HAARA hua (Ghazni se). Bhim II (bada number, baad mein, 1178) = JEETA\n(Ghori ko haraya) — number jitna bada, result utna behtar (I=lose, II=win) — is simple pattern se dono yaad rahenge.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠","Bhim I = Somnath (1025-26 CE) mein Ghazni se HAARA. Bhim II = Gujarat (1178 CE) mein Ghori ko HARAYA —\nGhori ki pehli haar. I aur II ko confuse mat karo.\n5. Muhammad Ghori — Poora Battle Record\n●1175CE: Multan+Kutch(1st invasion) · 1178CE: Gujarat mein Bhim II se HAARA (pehli haar)\n●1191CE(1st Tarain): Prithviraj se HAARA · 1192CE(2nd Tarain): Prithviraj ko HARAYA(decisive)\n●1194CE(Chandawar): Jayachandra ko HARAYA · 1205CE: Khokhar tribe(aakhri campaign)\n TRICK — \"Haar-Haar-Jeet-Jeet\" pattern trick\n💡\nGhori ka pattern: 1178=HAAR (Bhim II) → 1191=HAAR (Prithviraj) → 1192=JEET (Prithviraj) → 1194=JEET\n(Jayachandra). Pehle 2 baar haara, phir 2 baar jeeta — \"do haar, phir do jeet\" — is simple rhythm se poora timeline\nyaad rahega.\nSaal ke last digit se bhi trick nikalti hai: 8(1178)=haar, 1(1191)=haar, 2(1192)=jeet, 4(1194)=jeet — bas \"pehle do haar\nwale, baad ke do jeet wale\" yaad rakho.\n6. 3 Historians of Mahmud Ghazni\n●Utbi → Kitab-ul-Yamini\n●Firdausi → Shahnama (Persian EPIC POETRY, India ki history NAHI)\n●Al-Biruni → Tahqiq-i-Hind (=Kitab-ul-Hind) — India ke baare mein SABSE DETAILED\n TRICK — \"U-F-A\" historian trick\n💡\nUtbi=Yamini, Firdausi=Shahnama(poetry,not history), Al-Biruni=Hind(India-focused,sabse detailed) — teeno naam ke\npehle letter se apni book yaad rakho: U-F-A.\nFirdausi ko trap se bachao: uski Shahnama Persian POETRY hai, India ki history NAHI — baaki 2 (Utbi, Al-Biruni)\nhistory-focused hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nUtbi=Kitab-ul-Yamini. Al-Biruni=Tahqiq-i-Hind(=Kitab-ul-Hind). Firdausi=Shahnama (Persian epic POETRY, India\nhistory nahi) — teeno alag books, mix mat karo.\n7. 4 Slaves of Ghori — Territory Match\n●Tajuddin Yaldoz → Ghazni\n●Qutubuddin Aibak → Lahore+Delhi → Slave Dynasty(1206CE) — SABSE IMPORTANT\n●Nasiruddin Qubacha → Multan\n●Bakhtiyar Khilji → Bengal → Nalanda University DESTROY ki\n TRICK — \"YAQB\" slave-territory trick\n💡\nYaldoz-Ghazni, Aibak-Lahore/Delhi, Qubacha-Multan, Bakhtiyar-Bengal = \"YAQB\" — bolo \"Yaar Aibak Queen Bani\"\n(silly line, letters match ho jaayenge).\nNalanda destroyer = Bakhtiyar Khilji — cross-chapter link: Nalanda banayi thi Kumaragupta I ne (Gupta chapter),\naur destroy ki Bakhtiyar Khilji ne — ek hi jagah, do alag empires, dono extremes yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNalanda University destroy ki Bakhtiyar Khilji ne (Ghori ka slave, Bengal wala) — Muhammad Ghori ya Mahmud\nGhazni ne khud NAHI.\n8. Bonus — Chishti Sufi Order\n●Sheikh Moinuddin Chishti → Ghori ke saath India aaye · India mein Chishti Sufi Order ke founder · Dargah Ajmer,\nRajasthan","TRICK — \"Ghori ke saath aaya Sufi\" hook\n💡\nYaad rakho: Moinuddin Chishti Ghori ke saath hi aaye the — political invasion (Ghori) aur spiritual movement (Sufi)\ndono saath-saath shuru hue is period mein.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"First Muslim(group)=Arabs, individual=Qasim(712,Raja Dahir haraya) → Ghazni=Loot vs Ghori=Permanent Rule →\nGhazni:17 invasions,16th=Somnath(BhimI haara) → Ghori: 1178-haar(BhimII), 1191-haar(Prithviraj), 1192-jeet, 1194-\njeet(Jayachandra) → Historians: Utbi-Yamini,Firdausi-Shahnama(poetry),Al-Biruni-TahqiqiHind → Slaves:\nYAQB(Yaldoz-Ghazni,Aibak-Lahore/Delhi/1206CE,Qubacha-Multan,Bakhtiyar-Bengal/Nalanda destroy) → Sufi:\nMoinuddin Chishti-Ajmer\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Somnath = 16th invasion (NOT 17th) — total 17 invasions the.\n2) Bhim I=haara(Somnath,Ghazni se). Bhim II=jeeta(Gujarat,Ghori ki pehli haar).\n3) Nalanda destroyer = Bakhtiyar Khilji (Ghori ka slave), na ki Ghori ya Ghazni khud.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.1 Arab & Turk Invasions","DELHI SULTANATE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 2 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 5 Dynasties — Duration Ka Trap\n●Slave(1206-1290) = 84 saal, 11 rulers — PEHLI\n●Khilji(1290-1320) = 30 saal\n●Tughlaq(1320-1412) = 92 saal — SABSE LAMBI\n●Sayyid(1414-1451) = 37 saal\n●Lodi(1451-1526) = 75 saal — AAKHRI (Afghan dynasty)\n TRICK — \"SKTSL — 84-30-92-37-75\" trick\n💡\nOrder: Slave-Khilji-Tughlaq-Sayyid-Lodi = \"SKTSL\". Common galti: log sochte hain Slave(pehli) ya Lodi(aakhri)\nsabse lambi hogi — NAHI, Tughlaq(92 saal, beech ki dynasty) sabse lambi hai.\nYaad rakho: \"Tughlaq = Tug-of-war jaisa lamba khichaa\" — naam mein hi \"lamba khinchna\" jaisa sound hai, isse 92-\nsaal-longest fact lock ho jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTughlaq Dynasty (92 saal) = Delhi Sultanate ki SABSE LAMBI dynasty — Slave ya Lodi NAHI.\n2. Diwans (Departments) — Introducer Match\n●Diwan-e-Arz(Military) = Balban ne banaya\n●Diwan-e-Amir-Kohi(Agriculture) = Muhammad bin Tughlaq\n●Diwan-e-Khairat + Diwan-e-Bandagan + Dar-ul-shifa = Firoz Shah Tughlaq ne 3 banaye\n TRICK — \"1-1-3\" department-count trick\n💡\nBalban=1 department(Arz/military — Balban khud \"Blood and Iron\" tha, military-focused). Md bin Tughlaq=1 (Amir-\nKohi/agriculture — uske famous \"experiments\" mein se ek). Firoz Shah=3 departments (welfare-focused raja, isliye\nzyada departments) — \"jitna welfare-minded utne zyada departments\".\n3. Qutub Minar — Started vs Completed\n●Aibak → Qutub Minar START ki · Quwwat-ul-Islam Mosque + Adhai Din Ka Jhopra banwaya\n●Iltutmish → Qutub Minar COMPLETE ki (73 metres)\n●Aibak ki death: Chaugan(Polo) khelte hue, Lahore, 1210 CE — WAR mein NAHI\n TRICK — \"Start-Complete\" + Polo-death trick\n💡\nAibak = \"Aarambh\" (shuruaat) — Qutub Minar start ki. Iltutmish = \"Illil poora kiya\" (complete kiya, 73m) — bas \"A se\nstart, I se poora\" yaad rakho.\nAibak ki death = Polo (Chaugan) — ek badshah khel khelte hue mar gaya, war mein nahi — ye unique/ironic fact\nkhud hi yaad reh jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Qutub Minar kisne banayi?\" → Aibak ne START ki, Iltutmish ne COMPLETE ki (73m). \"Built\" ka seedha jawab\nAibak dena galat hai agar \"complete\" poocha jaaye.\n4. Turkan-i-Chahalgani & Razia Sultana\n●Iltutmish → 40 nobles ka group BANAYA (Turkan-i-Chahalgani)\n●Balban → usi group ko ABOLISH kiya","●Razia Sultana → Medieval India ki pehli Muslim mahila raja · Purdah reject kiya · Assassination: Kaithal(Haryana),\n13 Oct 1240, Khokhar tribe dwara — Delhi mein NAHI\n TRICK — \"Banaya vs Abolish\" + Razia-Kaithal trick\n💡\nIltutmish = \"Istart-Initiate\" (banaya) → Balban = \"Bal todna\" (bal/power todna, abolish kiya) — dono naam alag actions\nse match ho jaate hain (dono \"B\" se hi shuru nahi hote isliye easy distinguish).\nRazia ki death Kaithal mein hui, Delhi mein NAHI — yaad rakho: \"Kaithal mein Khokhar tribe ne Katal kiya\" —\nKa-Kh-Ka teeno sound se location aur culprit dono yaad reh jaate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTurkan-i-Chahalgani: Iltutmish ne BANAYA, Balban ne ABOLISH kiya. Razia ki assassination Kaithal(Haryana) mein\nhui, Delhi mein NAHI.\n5. Alauddin Khilji — Kohinoor Ka Sahi Jawab\n●Malik Kafur → Warangal campaign(1309CE) → Prataparudra Dev se Kohinoor diamond liya\n●Original naam: Ali Gurshasp · Title: Sikandar-e-Sani · Court poet Amir Khusro(Khazain-ul-Futuh)\n TRICK — \"Kohinoor = Warangal, NOT Gujarat/Chittor\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log Kohinoor ko Gujarat ya Chittor se jodte hain (kyunki wo bhi famous campaigns the) — GALAT.\nYaad rakho: \"Warangal mein Kafur ko kohinoor mila\" — \"Kafur\" aur \"Kohinoor\" dono \"K\" se, aur Warangal khud\n\"war\" se shuru hota hai (jaise treasure-war jeetne se mila).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKohinoor Diamond = Malik Kafur ne Warangal(1309CE) campaign mein Prataparudra Dev se liya — Gujarat ya Chittor\nse NAHI.\n6. Muhammad Bin Tughlaq — SAB Experiments FAILED\n●Doab Taxation(10x→20x) → rebellion\n●Capital Shift(Delhi→Devagiri) → FAILED, wapas shift\n●Token Currency(copper/brass) → FAILED (nakli sikke)\n●Karachil Campaign → bhaari nuksaan, FAILED\n TRICK — \"Sab Kuch Fail\" trick\n💡\nEk hi word yaad rakho poore raja ke liye: FAIL. Doab-fail, Capital shift-fail, Token currency-fail, Karachil-fail — 4\nmein se 4 FAILED, isliye hi unhe \"unfortunate/ill-fated\" raja kaha jaata hai. Koi bhi \"successful\" wala option agar aaye\nexam mein, wo galat hoga.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMuhammad bin Tughlaq ke SAARE major experiments (Capital Shift, Token Currency, Karachil Campaign, Doab\nTaxation) FAILED hue — koi bhi successful nahi tha.\n7. 2 Books \"Tarikh-i-Firozshahi\" — Author Trap\n●Ziauddin Barani ne likhi → Muhammad bin Tughlaq ke time par\n●Shams-i-Siraj Afif ne likhi → Firoz Shah Tughlaq ke time par\n TRICK — \"Barani=Juna, Afif=Firoz\" trick\n💡\nSame naam ki 2 books, 2 alag authors — yaad rakho pehla-letter match: Barani(pehle likha gaya author, alphabetically\nbhi B pehle) → Md bin Tughlaq(pehla/earlier raja). Afif(baad wala author) → Firoz Shah(baad wala raja). \"Pehla\nauthor-pehla raja, baad wala author-baad wala raja\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠","\"Tarikh-i-Firozshahi\" naam ki 2 books hain: Ziauddin Barani=Muhammad bin Tughlaq ke baare mein. Shams-i-Siraj\nAfif=Firoz Shah Tughlaq ke baare mein. Author+ruler dono match karo.\n8. Firoz Shah Tughlaq — \"Akbar of Sultanate Period\"\n●Elliot & Elphinstone ne title diya — Muhammad bin Tughlaq ko NAHI\n●Welfare works: Employment Bureau, Kisano ke Takavi loans maaf, PWD found ki, Land Revenue tax 1/5→1/3\n TRICK — \"Welfare = Akbar-jaisa\" trick\n💡\nFiroz = Welfare raja (jaise Akbar bhi welfare/tolerance ke liye jaana jaata hai) — isliye historians ne unhe \"Akbar of\nSultanate Period\" bola. Muhammad bin Tughlaq = Fail raja — welfare wala tag sirf Firoz ko milta hai, uske\npredecessor(Juna Khan) ko nahi.\n9. Agra & Delhi Sultanate Ka Ant\n●Agra = Sikandar Lodi ne 1504CE mein basaya, 1506 se capital — Babur/Akbar ne NAHI\n●First Battle of Panipat(21 April 1526) → Babur ne Ibrahim Lodi ko haraya → Delhi Sultanate khatam, Mughal\nEmpire shuru\n TRICK — \"Sikandar=Agra, Ibrahim=Last\" trick\n💡\nSikandar Lodi = \"Sikandar ne shehar basaya\" (Agra) — dusra Sikandar (Alexander) bhi conqueror+city-builder jaisa\ntha, wordplay se yaad rakho.\nIbrahim Lodi = last domino — Lodi dynasty ka bhi last, poori Delhi Sultanate ka bhi last, battlefield mein hi mara\ngaya (Sikandar Lodi ki maut normal thi) — \"Ibrahim = end of the line\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAgra basaya Sikandar Lodi ne (1504 CE) — Babur ya Akbar ne NAHI, ye common misconception hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"5 dynasties: SKTSL(84-30-92-37-75, Tughlaq longest) → Diwans: Arz-Balban, AmirKohi-MdbinTughlaq,\nKhairat/Bandagan/Darulshifa-FirozShah → Qutub Minar: Aibak-start,Iltutmish-complete(73m) → Aibak death=Polo →\nTurkan-i-Chahalgani: Iltutmish-banaya,Balban-abolish → Razia: Kaithal death → Kohinoor: MalikKafur-\nWarangal(1309) → MdbinTughlaq: sab experiments FAILED → 2 TarikhiFirozshahi: Barani-MdbinTughlaq, Afif-\nFirozShah → Firoz Shah=Akbar of Sultanate → Agra=SikandarLodi(1504) → Panipat(1526)=Babur beat IbrahimLodi\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Tughlaq(92 saal)=Sabse lambi dynasty — Slave ya Lodi nahi.\n2) Qutub Minar: Aibak=started, Iltutmish=completed(73m).\n3) Kohinoor Diamond = Malik Kafur ne Warangal(1309) se liya, Gujarat/Chittor se nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Delhi Sultanate","VIJAYANAGARA & BAHMANI EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK\nSHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Founders (2, Not 1!) + 4 Dynasties\n●Founders = Harihara I AUR Bukka (dono, sirf ek NAHI) — Kampili kingdom ke ex-ministers, 1336CE\n●Sangama(Harihara I) → Saluva(S.Narasimha) → Tuluva(Vir Narasimha, KDR yahin hai) →\nAravidu(Tirumala,last:Sriranga III)\n TRICK — \"2 Founders + STSA\" trick\n💡\nHarihara + Bukka = do bhai jaise mile founders — \"Har-Buk\" bolo, dono naam saath yaad rakhne ke liye.\n4 dynasty order: Sangama-Tuluva... wait, seedha: Sangama-Saluva-Tuluva-Aravidu = \"STSA\"(sequence thoda alag hai,\nbas yaad rakho S-S-T-A). Krishna Deva Raya = TULUVA, na ki Sangama (jo pehli/founding dynasty thi) — common\ngalti hai kyunki KDR itna famous hai log use founding dynasty se jod dete hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nVijayanagara founders = Harihara I AUR Bukka (dono). Krishna Deva Raya = Tuluva dynasty se the, Sangama se\nNAHI.\n2. Religion — State vs Personal\n●State religion = Shaivism\n●Krishna Deva Raya personally = Vaishnavism\n TRICK — \"State-Shiv, KDR-Vishnu\" trick\n💡\nYaad rakho: \"Rajya(state) Shiva ka bhakt, par Raja(KDR) khud Vishnu ka bhakt\" — ek hi empire mein 2 alag religious\nidentities, dono ko separately yaad rakho.\n3. Battle of Talikota (1565) — Ant Ki Ladai\n●Dusra naam: Rakkasa-Tangadi war · 23-25 Jan 1565\n●Vijayanagara: Sadasiva Raya(nominal raja) + Rama Raya(actual control minister) — HAARE\n●Confederation(4 sultanates): Ahmadnagar+Bijapur+Golkonda+Bidar — JEETE. Bahmani khud shamil NAHI\n(pehle hi toot chuka tha)\n TRICK — \"Raja naam ke liye, Minister kaam ke liye\" trick\n💡\nSadasiva Raya = naam ka raja (nominal), Rama Raya = kaam ka raja (actual control) — dono ek hi side pe the, par\npower alag logo ke haath mein — is unique political setup ko yaad rakho.\n4 sultanates jeete, Bahmani khud NAHI tha — kyunki Bahmani tab tak already 5 tukdo mein toot chuka tha, isliye\n\"confederation\" naam se pukara gaya, Bahmani naam se nahi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBattle of Talikota mein confederation = 4 sultanates (Ahmadnagar, Bijapur, Golkonda, Bidar) — Bahmani khud is\nconfederation ka hissa NAHI tha (pehle hi toot chuka tha).\n4. Krishna Deva Raya — Works & Titles\n●Amuktamalyada(Telugu) = Polity/raj-neeti · Jambavati Kalyanam(Sanskrit) = drama\n●Titles: Andhra Bhoja, Andhra Pitamaha, Abhinava Bhoja, Yavanraj Sthanacharya\n●Constructions: Hazara Rama Temple, Vithala Swami Temple, Hospet(wife ki yaad), Nagallapur(maa Nagaladevi ki\nyaad)","TRICK — \"Telugu-Politics, Sanskrit-Drama\" + Hospet-Nagallapur trick\n💡\nAmuktamalyada = \"Aam/Aam-janta ki bhasha (Telugu)\" for raj-neeti (practical politics ke liye local bhasha).\nJambavati Kalyanam = \"classical/Sanskrit\" — drama ke liye traditional bhasha.\nHospet = Patni ki yaad, Nagallapur = Maa ki yaad — dono cities family members ki memory mein, easy match: \"H\"\nfor \"Hamsafar(wife)\", \"Naga\" khud maa ke naam (Nagaladevi) mein hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmuktamalyada = TELUGU (polity). Jambavati Kalyanam = SANSKRIT (drama). Dono Krishna Deva Raya ki\nrachnayein hain, alag bhasha mein.\n5. Ashtadiggajas — Peddana Ki Title Trap\n●Allasani Peddana(#7) = \"Grandfather of Telugu poetry\" (Andhra Kavita Pitamaha) — Manucharita likhi\n●Tenali Ramakrishna(#2) = Humorist, sabse famous story-teller\n TRICK — \"Peddana ki Pitamaha ≠ Raja ki Pitamaha\" trick\n💡\nKDR ka title = \"Andhra Pitamaha\". Peddana ka title = \"Andhra Kavita Pitamaha\" — dono mein \"Pitamaha\"\ncommon hai isliye confuse hota hai, par Peddana ke title mein extra word \"Kavita\" (poetry) hai — \"Kavita wala\nPeddana ka hai, plain wala Raja ka\" — is ek extra word se hi dono alag ho jaate hain.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKrishna Deva Raya = \"Andhra Pitamaha\". Allasani Peddana = \"Andhra Kavita Pitamaha\" (Grandfather of Telugu\nPOETRY specifically) — dono alag titles, ek word ka farak.\n6. Bahmani Founder — 3 Naam, Ek Aadmi\n●Original: Zafar Khan\n●Nickname: Hasan Gangu\n●Ruler naam: Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah\n●Capital: Gulbarga(renamed Ahsanabad)\n TRICK — \"ZHA\" 3-naam trick\n💡\nZafar Khan(original) → Hasan Gangu(nickname) → Alaunddin Hasan Bahman Shah(ruler-title) = \"Z-H-A\" — bolo\n\"Zindagi Hamesha Aage badhti hai\" (ek naam se doosre naam tak, life-journey jaisa).\n7. Bahmani Capital Shift\n●Gulbarga(founder Alauddin Hasan ne banayi) → Bidar(Shihabuddin Ahmad Shah I ne shift ki)\n TRICK — \"Founder-Gulbarga, Shihab-Bidar\" trick\n💡\nFounder khud pehli capital banata hai (Gulbarga), aur baad ka raja(Shihabuddin) naya shift karta hai(Bidar) —\npattern har dynasty mein common hai (jaise Slave dynasty mein bhi Lahore→Delhi shift hua tha), isliye is pattern se\nyaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBahmani capital: Alauddin Hasan(founder) ne Gulbarga banayi. Shihabuddin Ahmad Shah I ne Bidar shift ki — galat\nruler se link mat karo.\n8. Gol Gumbaz vs Charminar — Builder Match\n●Gol Gumbaz = Muhammad Adil Shah(Bijapur) ne banaya\n●Ibrahim Adil Shah(Bijapur) = Kitab-e-Nauras likhi, Dakhani language promote ki — Gol Gumbaz NAHI banaya","●Charminar + Hyderabad(Bhagyanagar) = Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah(Golkonda) ne banaya\n TRICK — \"Same first name, alag kaam\" trick\n💡\n2 alag \"Muhammad\" naam ke rajaon ne 2 alag building banayi: Muhammad Adil Shah(Bijapur)=Gol Gumbaz,\nMuhammad Quli Qutb Shah(Golkonda)=Charminar. Naam same-ish hai (\"Muhammad\") par dynasty+building bilkul\nalag — surname (\"Adil\" vs \"Quli\") se differentiate karo.\nIbrahim Adil Shah ≠ Muhammad Adil Shah — dono Bijapur ke hain, par Ibrahim ne kitaab likhi (Kitab-e-Nauras),\nMuhammad ne building banayi (Gol Gumbaz).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGol Gumbaz = Muhammad Adil Shah (Bijapur), Ibrahim Adil Shah NAHI. Charminar+Hyderabad = Muhammad Quli\nQutb Shah (Golkonda, alag dynasty).\n9. 5 Deccan States — Oldest, Newest, Merge\n●Berar(1484,oldest) → Ahmadnagar(1574) mein merge\n●Bijapur(1489) → Mughal-Aurangzeb(1686) ne annex kiya\n●Ahmadnagar(1490) → Mughal-Shah Jahan(1636) ne annex kiya\n●Golkonda(1512) → Mughal-Aurangzeb(1687) ne annex kiya\n●Bidar(1526,newest) → Bijapur(1619) mein merge\n TRICK — \"Berar oldest, Bidar newest\" trick\n💡\nFounded order: 1484(Berar)→1489(Bijapur)→1490(Ahmadnagar)→1512(Golkonda)→1526(Bidar) — Berar sabse\npurana, Bidar sabse naya.\nAurangzeb ne 2 liye(Bijapur+Golkonda), Shah Jahan ne 1(Ahmadnagar) — \"Aurangzeb ne do haath se do state\nliye\" — number se yaad rakho: Aurangzeb=2, Shah Jahan=1.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSabse purana Deccan state = Berar(1484). Sabse naya = Bidar(1526). Aurangzeb ne Bijapur(1686)+Golkonda(1687)\nannex kiye; Shah Jahan ne Ahmadnagar(1636) annex kiya.\n10. Foreign Travelers — Kaun Kiske Time Aaya\n●Nicolo Conti(Italy) → Devaraya I(1420CE)\n●Abdur Razzaq(Persia) → Devaraya II\n●Paes + Barbosa(Portuguese) → Krishna Deva Raya\n●Fernao Nuniz(Portuguese) → Achyuta Deva Raya\n TRICK — \"2 Devarayas, 2 travelers\" trick\n💡\nDevaraya I → Conti(dono naam \"I\"/\"o\" sound se end hote hain lagbhag). Devaraya II → Razzaq. Number I-II se\ntravelers alphabetically bhi roughly match karte hain (C before R).\nKDR ke time 2 Portuguese aaye(Paes+Barbosa) — sabse famous raja ke time sabse zyada travelers, naturally bhi sahi\nlagta hai (bada raja=zyada visitors).\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Founders: Harihara I+Bukka(1336) → 4 dynasty: Sangama-Saluva-Tuluva(KDR)-Aravidu → Religion: State-\nShaivism,KDR-Vaishnavism → Talikota(1565): SadasivaRaya+RamaRaya haare, 4 sultanates jeete(Bahmani nahi) →\nKDR: Amuktamalyada(Telugu)-JambavatiKalyanam(Sanskrit), Andhra Pitamaha → Peddana=Andhra KAVITA\nPitamaha(alag) → Bahmani founder: ZafarKhan-HasanGangu-AlauddinHasanBahmanShah → Capital:\nGulbarga(founder)-Bidar(Shihabuddin) → GolGumbaz=MdAdilShah, Charminar=MdQuliQutbShah → 5 Deccan:\nBerar(oldest)-Bidar(newest), Aurangzeb=2states,ShahJahan=1 → Travelers: Conti-DevarayaI, Razzaq-DevarayaII,\nPaes/Barbosa-KDR, Nuniz-AchyutaDevaRaya\"","Roz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Founders=Harihara I AUR Bukka (dono). KDR=Tuluva dynasty, Sangama nahi.\n2) Battle of Talikota: confederation=4 sultanates, Bahmani khud shamil nahi tha.\n3) Gol Gumbaz=Muhammad Adil Shah. Charminar/Hyderabad=Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah — do alag 'Muhammad'\nrajaon ke do alag buildings.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.3 Vijayanagara & Bahmani Empire","BHAKTI & SUFI MOVEMENT — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Saguna vs Nirguna — Guru-Shishya Ka Twist\n●Saguna(Roop wala) → Ramananda, Surdas, Meerabai, Tulsidas, Chaitanya\n●Nirguna(Nirakar) → Kabirdas, Guru Nanak, Dadu Dayal\n●Ramananda(Saguna) ka shishya Kabirdas(Nirguna) — guru-shishya mein philosophy badal gayi\n TRICK — \"Roop vs Nirakar\" + guru-shishya-twist trick\n💡\nSaguna = \"Sa+Guna\"(guno/attributes ke SAATH) → roop wala bhagwan. Nirguna = \"Nir+Guna\"(guno ke\nBINA/nirakar) → formless. Naam mein hi \"sa/nir\" (with/without) ka meaning chhupa hai.\nRamananda(Saguna) → Kabir(Nirguna) — unique example jahan guru ek tarah ka tha, shishya doosri tarah ka ban\ngaya. Ye exact combo yaad rakho: \"Guru roop wala tha, shishya nirakar ban gaya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKabirdas aur Guru Nanak = NIRGUNA. Ramananda, Meerabai, Surdas, Tulsidas = SAGUNA. Ramananda khud Saguna\nthe lekin unke shishya Kabir Nirguna the.\n2. Adi Shankaracharya — 4 Mathas\n●North=Badrinath · East=Puri · West=Dwarka · South=Sringeri\n●Philosophy: Advaita Vedanta · Kitaab: Brahmasutra Bhashya · Smarta Tradition develop ki\n TRICK — \"N-E-W-S\" compass trick\n💡\nCompass directions se seedha match: North-Badrinath, East-Puri, West-Dwarka, South-Sringeri. Bas actual India ka\nmap yaad karo — Badrinath Himalaya(N) mein hai, Puri Odisha(E) mein, Dwarka Gujarat(W) mein, Sringeri\nKarnataka(S) mein — geography se hi lock ho jaata hai.\n3. Meerabai Ka Guru — Chain Yaad Rakho\n●Ramananda → Raidas(Ravidas) → Meerabai\n●Ramananda directly Meerabai ka guru NAHI tha\n TRICK — \"3-generation chain\" trick\n💡\nEk seedhi(ladder) socho: Ramananda(top) → Raidas(middle) → Meerabai(bottom). Meerabai ka SEEDHA guru\nRaidas hai, Ramananda uska \"guru ka guru\" hai — teen level ki chain, skip mat karo beech wala.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMeerabai ka DIRECT guru = Raidas (Ravidas), na ki Ramananda. Ramananda-Raidas-Meerabai — teen-level chain hai.\n4. Bhavartha-Deepika vs Bhavarth Ramayana\n●Bhavartha-Deepika(Gita commentary, Marathi) = Gyaneshwar\n●Bhavarth Ramayana(Ramayana commentary) = Eknath\n TRICK — \"Deepika=Gita, Ramayana=Ramayana\" trick\n💡\nBook naam mein hi doosra text ka naam hai — Bhavarth RAMAYANA = seedha Ramayana ki commentary (Eknath\nne likhi). Bhavartha-DEEPIKA = \"deepika\" (lamp/light) jaisa naam Gita ke gyaan-prakash se match karta hai\n(Gyaneshwar ne likhi) — dono authors ke naam mein bhi \"G\" wala pattern hai jo Gita se hi shuru karta hai\n(Gyaneshwar-Gita).","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBhavartha-Deepika (Gita commentary) = Gyaneshwar. Bhavarth Ramayana (Ramayana commentary) = Eknath. Naam\nsimilar lagte hain par alag authors, alag texts.\n5. 7 Major Philosophies — Suffix Trap\n●Advaita=Shankaracharya · Vishishtadvaita=Ramanujacharya · Dvaitadvaita=Nimbarkacharya\n●Shuddhadvaita=Vallabhacharya · Dvaita=Madhvacharya · Achintya Bhedabheda=Chaitanya · Shaiva\nVishishtadvaita=Shrikantha\n TRICK — \"AVDSD-ACS\" philosophy trick\n💡\nSuffix dekh ke confuse mat ho — sab \"-dvaita/-advaita\" hain par har naam ek SPECIFIC philosopher se juda hai. Yaad\nrakho ek chain: \"Advaita-Shankaracharya, Vishishtadvaita-Ramanuja, Dvaitadvaita-Nimbarka, Shuddhadvaita-\nVallabha, Dvaita-Madhva\" — pehla-syllable(A,Vi,Dvaita,Shuddha,Dvaita) se philosopher yaad rakho, na ki poora\nnaam.\nChaitanya = Achintya Bhedabheda (ye \"dvaita/advaita\" suffix use NAHI karta, isliye alag pehchan aasan hai).\n6. Chishti Order — Oldest, NOT Largest\n●India ka SABSE PURANA(oldest) Sufi Order — sabse bada(largest) NAHI\n●Founder Muinuddin Chishti → Khanqah AJMER mein (Delhi mein NAHI)\n●Nizamuddin Auliya(Chishti) = Mehboob-e-Ilahi · Disciple Amir Khusrau(poet-musician)\n TRICK — \"Oldest≠Largest\" + Ajmer trick\n💡\nChishti = SABSE PEHLA aaya (isliye oldest), par baad mein doosre orders bhi bade ho gaye — \"pehla aana\" aur\n\"sabse bada hona\" alag baatein hain, is distinction ko yaad rakho.\nMuinuddin Chishti = Ajmer — pehle bhi (Ch.1 Medieval, Arab/Turk Invasions mein) yaad kiya tha ki ye Ghori ke\nsaath India aaye the, dargah Ajmer mein hai — cross-chapter consistency check karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChishti Order = India ka SABSE PURANA Sufi Order (largest NAHI). Muinuddin Chishti ka Khanqah AJMER mein\ntha, Delhi mein NAHI.\n7. Tansen Ka Guru — Shattari Order\n●Muhammad Ghaus(Shattari Order, title \"Qutb\") = Tansen ke Guru — Nizamuddin Auliya NAHI\n TRICK — \"Ghaus=Music Guru\" trick\n💡\nMuhammad Ghaus naam mein \"Ghaus\" sound \"Ghazal/music\" jaisa hai — isse Tansen(music legend) ka guru yaad\nrakhna easy ho jaata hai. Nizamuddin Auliya = Amir Khusrau ka guru tha, Tansen ka NAHI — dono \"famous musician-\nconnected sufi\" lagte hain isliye confuse hota hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTansen ka guru = Muhammad Ghaus (Shattari Order). Nizamuddin Auliya (Chishti Order) = Amir Khusrau ka guru tha\n— dono alag hain.\n8. 6 Sufi Orders — Founder + Key Figure\n●Chishti(Muinuddin Chishti,oldest) · Shattari(Shah Abdullah,Tansen's guru Muhammad Ghaus)\n●Firdausi(Sheikh Badruddin, Suhrawardi ki BRANCH) · Naqshbandi(Bahauddin Naqshband, India mein Ahmad\nSirhindi)\n●Suhrawardi(Shihabuddin Suhrawardi) · Qadiri(Abdul Qadir Gilani, follower Dara Shikoh)","TRICK — \"CSFNSQ\" 6-order trick\n💡\nChishti-Shattari-Firdausi-Naqshbandi-Suhrawardi-Qadiri = \"CSFNSQ\" — koi bhi silly sentence bana lo letters se, jaise\n\"Chai Se Fresh Na Soyi Qismat\".\nFirdausi = Suhrawardi ki hi BRANCH — ye ek is-poore-list mein akela \"sub-order\" hai, baaki sab independent orders\nhain. Qadiri = Dara Shikoh (Mughal prince, Aurangzeb ka bhai) — is royal-connection se yaad rakho.\n9. Sattriya Dance — Shankaradeva (Assam)\n●Shankaradeva(Assam) → Sattriya dance ke founder · Bhakti Assam mein start ki · Borgeets tradition\n TRICK — \"Assam-Sattriya\" hook\n💡\nShankaradeva-Sattriya — dono \"S\" se, Assam ka apna unique dance form (Bharatnatyam/Kathak se confuse mat karo —\nwo alag regions/founders ke hain).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSattriya dance ka founder = Shankaradeva (Assam), na ki Bharatnatyam/Kathak ka koi founder — ye alag classical\ndance forms hain.\n10. Top 5 Sufi Terms\n●Chilla = 40-din meditation · Khanqah = Sufi residence · Fana = Khuda ke prem mein dubna\n●Sama = Music-dance spiritual practice · Wahdat-ul-Wujud = Monism(oneness)\n TRICK — \"CKFSW\" term-meaning trick\n💡\nChilla=40 din (number yaad rakho), Khanqah=ghar/residence, Fana=dubna/immersion, Sama=music, Wahdat-ul-\nWujud=Wujud(existence)=Monism/oneness — last term ka naam khud hi \"ekta/wujud\" bata deta hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Saguna(Ramananda-Surdas-Meera-Tulsi-Chaitanya) vs Nirguna(Kabir-Nanak-Dadu) →\nShankaracharya:4Mathas(NEWS) → Meerabai guru-chain: Ramananda-Raidas-Meerabai → Gyaneshwar(Bhavartha-\nDeepika,Gita) vs Eknath(Bhavarth Ramayana) → 7 philosophies: Advaita-Shankaracharya,Vishishtadvaita-\nRamanuja,Dvaitadvaita-Nimbarka,Shuddhadvaita-Vallabha,Dvaita-Madhva,AchintyaBhedabheda-Chaitanya →\nChishti=oldest(Ajmer,not largest) → Nizamuddin Auliya-Amir Khusrau vs Muhammad Ghaus-Tansen → 6 orders:\nCSFNSQ → Shankaradeva=Sattriya(Assam) → Terms: Chilla-40din,Khanqah-residence,Fana-immersion,Sama-\nmusic,Wahdat-ul-Wujud-monism\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Kabirdas aur Guru Nanak = Nirguna; Ramananda/Meerabai/Surdas/Tulsidas = Saguna.\n2) Meerabai ka guru = Raidas (Ramananda ka shishya), na ki Ramananda directly.\n3) Chishti Order = oldest (largest NAHI), Ajmer mein (Delhi nahi). Tansen ka guru = Muhammad Ghaus (Shattari),\nNizamuddin Auliya nahi.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Bhakti & Sufi Movement","MUGHAL EMPIRE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 5 (Highest Weightage) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Babur = Founder, Akbar = Real Founder\n●Babur = Founder(1526) · Akbar = REAL/Actual Founder — same pattern as Gupta(Shri Gupta vs Chandragupta I)\n●Baburnama = Chagatai TURKISH mein likhi (Persian/Arabic NAHI) · Persian translation: Abdur Rahim Khan-i-\nKhana · English: Annette Beveridge\n TRICK — \"Cross-chapter pattern\" trick\n💡\nYe BILKUL same pattern hai jo Gupta chapter mein tha: \"Shri Gupta=founder, Chandragupta I=real founder\" →\nyahan \"Babur=founder, Akbar=real founder\". Ek hi memory-hook dono chapters ke liye use karo.\nBaburnama = Babur ki Boli (Chagatai Turkish, uski matribhasha) mein likha — obvious hai ki khud ki autobiography\nkhud ki bhasha mein likhega, Persian/Arabic uski mother tongue nahi thi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBabur = Founder. Akbar = Real/Actual Founder. Baburnama = Chagatai Turkish mein (Persian/Arabic NAHI) —\nPersian translation baad mein Abdur Rahim ne ki.\n2. Babur Ke 4 Battles — PAN-KHA-CHA-GHA\n●Panipat(1526,Ibrahim Lodi) → Tulughma formation + Ottoman artillery pehli baar use\n●Khanwa(1527,Rana Sanga) → Ghazi title + alcohol ban + Tamgha tax khatam\n●Chanderi(1528,Medini Rai) → Rajput mahilaon ne Jauhar kiya\n●Ghagra(1529,Afghans) → Permanent control India par mila\n TRICK — \"PAN-KHA-CHA-GHA\" trick (source ka apna mnemonic)\n💡\n\"Babur ne PANi piya, KHAna khaya, phir CHAdar odh kar, GHAr gaya\" — PAN=Panipat, KHA=Khanwa,\nCHA=Chanderi, GHA=Ghagra. Har battle ke baad ek naya action: Tulughma(Panipat)-Ghazi(Khanwa)-\nJauhar(Chanderi)-Permanent control(Ghagra).\n3. Humayun's Death & Sher Shah's Purana Qila\n●Humayun ki death: Dinpanah(Library) ki seedhiyon se girke — WAR mein NAHI, 1556CE\n●Purana Qila = Sher Shah Suri ne banaya (Humayun ki Dinpanah ko todkar) — Humayun ne NAHI\n TRICK — \"Library se giri, Qila Sher Shah ne banaya\" trick\n💡\nLane-Poole ne Humayun ke baare mein kaha: \"tumbled through life and tumbled out of it\" — 'tumbled'(girna) = literal\ndeath bhi (seedhiyon se girkar mara)! Ek hi word life aur death dono describe karta hai — ye unique quote-fact khud\nyaad reh jaata hai.\nSher Shah ne Humayun ki hi building(Dinpanah) ko TODKAR apna Purana Qila banaya — \"dushman ki cheez tod\nke apni banayi\" — is political-symbolism se yaad rakho ki QILA Sher Shah ka hai, Humayun ka nahi.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nHumayun ki death Dinpanah(library) ki seedhiyon se girke hui, kisi battle mein NAHI. Purana Qila Sher Shah Suri ne\nbanaya (Humayun ki Dinpanah todkar), Humayun ne khud NAHI.\n4. Ain-i-Dahsala vs Ain-i-Akbari\n●Ain-i-Dahsala(1580) = Todar Mal ka Land Revenue System\n●Ain-i-Akbari = Abul Fazl ki Akbarnama ka 3rd part (Akbarnama ki \"soul\")","TRICK — \"Dahsala=Dus, Akbari=Akbar-ki-kitaab\" trick\n💡\nDahsala = \"Dah(10)\" — 10-saal ki average paidawar ka calculation, Todar Mal ka land-revenue formula. Akbari =\nseedha \"Akbar-naama\" ka hi hissa — naam mein hi \"Akbar ki kitaab\" bata diya, isse Abul Fazl se link ho jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAin-i-Dahsala = Todar Mal ka land revenue system (1580). Ain-i-Akbari = Abul Fazl ki Akbarnama ka 3rd part — dono\nbilkul alag cheezein hain.\n5. Ibadat Khana(1575) vs Din-i-Ilahi(1582)\n●Ibadat Khana(1575, Fatehpur Sikri) = inter-religious dialogue centre — 1582 mein band\n●Din-i-Ilahi(1582) = Akbar ka naya \"dharm\" (Tauhid-e-Ilahi)\n TRICK — \"7-saal gap\" trick\n💡\nIbadat Khana(1575) BAND hui usi saal jab Din-i-Ilahi(1582) SHURU hua — 7 saal ka gap, ek khatam hote hi\ndoosra shuru — \"baat-cheet(dialogue) khatam, naya dharm shuru\". Yaad rakho: dialogue centre PEHLE aaya(1575),\nnaya religion BAAD mein(1582).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nIbadat Khana(1575)=dialogue centre, band 1582 mein. Din-i-Ilahi(1582)=naya dharm. Dono alag cheezein, 7 saal ka\ngap.\n6. Tansen Ka Guru & Nur Jahan Ka Naam\n●Tansen asli naam Ramtanu Pandey · Guru Muhammad Ghaus(Shattari Order) — Nizamuddin Auliya NAHI (Bhakti-\nSufi chapter se yaad karo)\n●Nur Jahan asli naam Mehrunnisa · Pita Itimad-ud-Daula(asli naam Ghiyas Beg) · Uska tomb Agra mein — Pietra\nDura ka earliest FULL use\n TRICK — Cross-chapter callback trick\n💡\nTansen-Muhammad Ghaus — ye EXACT SAME fact Bhakti-Sufi chapter mein bhi tha, isliye do chapters mein cross-\nverify ho jaata hai, bhoolna mushkil.\nNur Jahan = \"Prakash ki Duniya\" (naam ka matlab) — par uska ASLI naam Mehrunnisa hai, Nur Jahan sirf ek\nTITLE hai jo Jahangir ne diya — \"title ≠ asli naam\" pattern yaad rakho.\n7. Guru Arjan Dev vs Guru Tegh Bahadur — Kisne Kise Maara\n●Guru Arjan Dev(5th Guru) → JAHANGIR ne execute kiya (Khusrau rebellion mein saath dene ke liye)\n●Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th Guru) → AURANGZEB ne execute kiya (Islam accept karne se mana kiya)\n TRICK — \"5th=Jahangir, 9th=Aurangzeb\" trick\n💡\nGuru number aur Mughal raja dono timeline mein match karte hain: 5th Guru(earlier) = Jahangir(earlier raja), 9th\nGuru(baad mein) = Aurangzeb(baad ka raja) — dono \"pehle wala-pehle wala, baad wala-baad wala\" pattern se lock\nho jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGuru Arjan Dev = Jahangir ne execute kiya. Guru Tegh Bahadur = Aurangzeb ne execute kiya. Bahut common exam\ntrap — number(5th/9th) se raja match karo.\n8. Kohinoor Diamond — Poori Journey\n●Kakatiya dynasty(Golconda) mein originally · Malik Kafur laaya Warangal(1309) se\n●Golkonda-Shahjahan treaty(1636) mein Jumla ne gift kiya · Baad mein Nadir Shah(Persia) ne loota","TRICK — \"4-stop journey\" trick\n💡\nKohinoor ka safar ek 4-stop train jaisa socho: Kakatiya(origin) → Malik Kafur(1309,laya Delhi) → Jumla-\nShahjahan gift(1636) → Nadir Shah(loota). Har stop pe ek naya \"malik\", ye pura chain yaad rakho, ek bhi step skip\nmat karo.\n9. Dagh & Huliya System — Original Inventor\n●Alauddin Khilji(original inventor) → Sher Shah Suri(revived) → Akbar(bhi use kiya)\n TRICK — \"3 rajaon ne use kiya, sirf ek ne banaya\" trick\n💡\n3 alag rajaon ke naam is system se juda hai — par sirf Alauddin Khilji ORIGINAL inventor hai, baaki do (Sher Shah,\nAkbar) ne sirf use/revive kiya. \"Banane wala sirf ek, chalane wale kayi\" — pattern yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nDagh aur Huliya system originally Alauddin Khilji ne banaya (Delhi Sultanate chapter se). Sher Shah ne revive kiya,\nAkbar ne bhi use kiya — original credit Alauddin ka hai.\n10. Key Sources — Author Match\n●Baburnama(Babur,Chagatai) · Humayun-nama(Gulbadan Begum) · Akbarnama(Abul Fazl,3-parts,Part3=Ain-i-\nAkbari)\n●Tabaqat-i-Akbari(Nizamuddin Ahmad) · Tuzuk-i-Jahangiri(Jahangir khud, Persian, autobiography)\n TRICK — Emperor-vs-Courtier author trick\n💡\nKhud-likhi(Babur-Baburnama, Jahangir-Tuzuk) vs Doosre ne likhi(Humayun-nama by Gulbadan Begum(behen),\nAkbarnama by Abul Fazl(courtier)) — jinhone khud likhi wo \"autobiography\", baaki \"biography by someone else\".\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Babur=founder,Akbar=real founder → Baburnama=Chagatai Turkish → 4 battles: PAN-KHA-CHA-GHA(Tulughma-\nGhazi-Jauhar-PermanentControl) → Humayun death=library seedhi → Sher Shah=Purana Qila(NOT Humayun) → Ain-\ni-Dahsala(TodarMal,revenue) vs Ain-i-Akbari(AbulFazl,Akbarnama pt3) → Ibadat Khana(1575)→Din-i-Ilahi(1582) →\nTansen guru=Muhammad Ghaus, Nur Jahan=Mehrunnisa → Guru Arjan Dev-Jahangir, Guru Tegh Bahadur-Aurangzeb\n→ Kohinoor: Kakatiya-MalikKafur(1309)-Jumla gift(1636)-NadirShah loot → Dagh/Huliya: Alauddin(original)-\nSherShah(revive)-Akbar(use)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye SABSE ZYADA weightage wala chapter hai, isko sabse zyada baar dohrao.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Guru Arjan Dev=Jahangir ne execute kiya. Guru Tegh Bahadur=Aurangzeb ne execute kiya — swap mat karo.\n2) Purana Qila = Sher Shah Suri ne banaya (Humayun ki Dinpanah todkar), Humayun ne khud nahi.\n3) Ain-i-Dahsala=Todar Mal(revenue system). Ain-i-Akbari=Abul Fazl(Akbarnama ka part) — dono alag.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Mughal Empire (Highest Weightage)","PROVINCIAL DYNASTIES — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. 5 Provinces — Bengal Sabse Pehla Azad\n●Bengal(1338CE) = Delhi se PEHLA azad province — Jaunpur/Malwa/Kashmir/Gujarat sab BAAD mein\n●Order: Bengal(1338) → Malwa(1401) → Gujarat(1407) → Jaunpur, Kashmir\n TRICK — \"Bengal = No.1\" trick\n💡\nYaad rakho: \"Bengal Bola Bye-bye sabse pehle\" — B se shuru hone wala hi sabse pehle azad hua (1338), coincidence\nnahi, bas is wordplay se lock kar do.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBengal(1338 CE) = Delhi se sabse pehle azad hone wala province — Jaunpur ya Malwa NAHI.\n2. Key Nicknames — Direct Match\n●Shiraz of India = Jaunpur (sheher)\n●Akbar of Kashmir / Budshah = Zain-ul-Abidin\n●Siraj-e-Hind = Ibrahim Shah Sharqi\n●Malik-us-Sharq(Eastern ruler) = Malik Sarwar\n●Begada = Mahmud Begada(Gujarat, 2-forts)\n TRICK — \"Nickname list\" chain trick\n💡\nEk line mein sab: \"Jaunpur=Shiraz, Zain-ul-Abidin=Akbar-of-Kashmir/Budshah, Ibrahim=Siraj-e-Hind,\nSarwar=Malik-us-Sharq, Mahmud=Begada\" — bas ye 5 pairs bolke ratt lo, sab direct-match questions ban jaate hain.\n3. Jaunpur — Founded By vs Named After\n●City founded by = Firoz Shah Tughlaq\n●Naam rakha gaya = Muhammad bin Tughlaq(Jauna Khan) ke naam par — \"Jaunpur\" = \"Jauna+pur\"\n TRICK — \"Banane wala alag, naam wala alag\" trick\n💡\nJaise koi bacha ho jiska naam dada ke naam pe rakha jaaye, par paalne wala koi aur ho — Firoz Shah ne SHEHAR\nbanaya(palan-poshan), naam Muhammad bin Tughlaq(Jauna Khan) ka diya(tribute) — dono Tughlaq hi hain par\nrole alag: builder vs namesake.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nJaunpur city founded by Firoz Shah Tughlaq, LEKIN naam Muhammad bin Tughlaq (Jauna Khan) ke naam par rakha\ngaya — dono alag roles hain.\n4. 3 Famous Mosques — Builder Match\n●Adina Mosque(Bengal) = Sikandar Shah(Bengal ka raja)\n●Atala Mosque(1408)(Jaunpur) = Ibrahim Shah Sharqi\n●Jama Masjid Jaunpur(1470) = Hussain Shah Sharqi\n TRICK — \"Alag province, alag raja\" trick\n💡\n3 mosques, 3 alag province/raja combos — Adina=Bengal(Sikandar), Atala=Jaunpur early(Ibrahim,1408), Jama\nMasjid Jaunpur=Jaunpur later(Hussain,1470) — Jaunpur ki 2 mosques ko bhi date se yaad rakho:\n1408(pehla,Ibrahim) → 1470(baad mein,Hussain).","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAdina Mosque(Bengal)=Sikandar Shah. Atala Mosque(Jaunpur,1408)=Ibrahim Shah Sharqi. Jama Masjid\nJaunpur(1470)=Hussain Shah Sharqi — 3 alag builders.\n5. Kashmir — Sikandar Shah vs Zain-ul-Abidin\n●Sikandar Shah(Butshikan) = Sati BAN kiya · Max forced Hindu conversions · orthodox\n●Zain-ul-Abidin(Budshah) = Sati ban REVOKE kiya · Jizya+cow-slaughter BAN · \"Akbar of Kashmir\" · liberal\n TRICK — \"Sikandar=Ban, Zain=Un-ban\" trick\n💡\nEk raja ne rule LAGAYA, doosre ne WAPAS HATA diya — \"Sikandar Sakht(orthodox), Zain Zyada-liberal\" —\ndono naam ke pehle letter se hi personality yaad rakho: Sikandar=Sakht, Zain=Zyada-tolerant.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nSikandar Shah(Butshikan) = Sati BAN kiya (orthodox). Zain-ul-Abidin = Sati ban REVOKE kiya (liberal, 'Akbar of\nKashmir') — opposite actions, confuse mat karo.\n6. Gujarat — Founder vs Real Founder (Gupta/Mughal Jaisa Pattern)\n●Zafar Khan(Muzzafar Shah I) = Founder(1407)\n●Ahmed Shah = REAL Founder(1411) → Ahmedabad(1413) basayi — Zafar Khan ne NAHI\n TRICK — \"3rd repeat of same pattern\" trick\n💡\nYe pattern ab 3rd baar dekh rahe ho: Gupta(Shri Gupta/Chandragupta I), Mughal(Babur/Akbar), aur ab Gujarat(Zafar\nKhan/Ahmed Shah) — jab bhi \"founder vs real founder\" sawaal aaye, dusra naam wala hamesha city/stability laata hai.\nAhmed Shah = Ahmedabad — naam mein hi seedha match hai (Ahmed-Ahmedabad), yaad rakhna sabse easy hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nZafar Khan(Muzzafar Shah I) = Founder(1407). Ahmed Shah = Real Founder(1411) — Ahmedabad usne basayi, Zafar\nKhan ne nahi.\n7. Mahmud Begada — \"Be\" Matlab Do\n●2 forts jeete: Girnar Durg(1466) + Champaner Durg(1486) → isliye title \"Begada\"(\"Be\"=do)\n TRICK — \"Be=2\" trick\n💡\nBegada mein \"Be\" khud Persian/Urdu mein \"do\" ka matlab deta hai — 2 forts jeetne se ye title mila, EK fort se nahi.\nYaad rakho: \"Be-gada = 2-gada(fort)\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMahmud Begada ka title 2 FORTS jeetne se mila (Girnar+Champaner), ek fort se nahi — \"Be\" ka matlab \"do\" hai.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Bengal(1338,first) → Nicknames: Jaunpur-Shiraz, ZainulAbidin-Akbar of Kashmir/Budshah, Ibrahim-Siraj-e-Hind,\nSarwar-Malik-us-Sharq, Mahmud-Begada → Jaunpur: Firoz Shah founded, named after Jauna Khan(Md bin Tughlaq)\n→ Mosques: Adina(Bengal-Sikandar), Atala(1408-Ibrahim), JamaMasjid(1470-Hussain) → Kashmir: Sikandar-Sati ban,\nZain-Sati unban(liberal) → Gujarat: ZafarKhan(founder)-AhmedShah(real founder,Ahmedabad) → Begada: 2\nforts(Girnar+Champaner)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.","Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Bengal(1338) = Delhi se pehla azad province — Jaunpur/Malwa nahi.\n2) Kashmir: Sikandar Shah=Sati BAN kiya. Zain-ul-Abidin=Sati ban REVOKE kiya (opposite).\n3) Gujarat: Zafar Khan=Founder(1407). Ahmed Shah=Real Founder(1411,Ahmedabad basayi).\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Provincial Dynasties","LATER MUGHAL PERIOD — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nMedieval History · Chapter 7 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Rulers Ke Nicknames — Weak Successors\n●Bahadur Shah I = Shah-e-Bekhbar(Unaware King)\n●Jahandar Shah = Lampat Moorkh, Laparwah\n●Farrukhsiyar = Ghranit Kayar(Notorious Coward)\n●Muhammad Shah = Rangila Badshah — sirf positive-sounding naam, par unke time Nadir Shah invasion hua\n TRICK — \"Sab weak, ek 'positive' lekin disaster\" trick\n💡\nSab nicknames NEGATIVE hain(Bekhbar-unaware, Moorkh-foolish, Kayar-coward) — SIRF Rangila\nBadshah(Muhammad Shah) positive lagta hai, par yehi wo raja hai jiske time Nadir Shah ne Delhi loot li — \"positive\nnaam wale ke time hi sabse bada disaster hua\", ye irony yaad rakho.\n2. Jizya Tax — On-Off-Off Pattern\n●Jahandar Shah → Jizya ABOLISH\n●Farrukhsiyar → Jizya RESTORE\n●Muhammad Shah(1720) → Jizya FINALLY abolish (permanent)\n TRICK — \"Off-On-Off\" trick\n💡\nSequence: Off(Jahandar) → On(Farrukhsiyar) → Off-Permanent(Muhammad Shah). \"Finally abolished\" ka\nanswer HAMESHA Muhammad Shah hai — koi aur nahi, ye directly poocha jaata hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n\"Jizya finally/permanently abolished\" = Muhammad Shah (1720). Jahandar Shah=abolish(pehli baar),\nFarrukhsiyar=restore — teeno alag actions.\n3. Sayyid Brothers — Kingmakers\n●Sayyid Brothers = Kingmakers(Khargonebar) · 1713-1720 CE administration control\n●Farrukhsiyar ko power diya, baad mein khud hi hataya bhi\n TRICK — \"Banaya aur bigada dono\" trick\n💡\nKingmakers naam khud bata deta hai — \"king BANANE\" wale, par yaad rakho wahi Farrukhsiyar ko baad mein\nhataya bhi — \"jisne banaya, usi ne bigada\" — makers hi breakers bhi ban gaye.\n4. Nadir Shah Invasion(1739) — DONO Liye\n●Battle of Karnal(1739) → Muhammad Shah haare\n●Nadir Shah le gaye: Peacock Throne(Takht-e-Taus) AUR Kohinoor Diamond — dono, sirf ek nahi\n TRICK — \"2 cheezein, ek nahi\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log sochte hain sirf ek cheez li — NAHI, DONO li: Peacock Throne + Kohinoor. Yaad rakho: \"Nadir\nne Nadir(rare) do cheezein churayi\" — dono precious items ek saath gaye, is completeness ko yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nNadir Shah(1739, Battle of Karnal) ne Peacock Throne AUR Kohinoor Diamond DONO liye, sirf ek nahi.","5. Battle of Buxar(1764) vs Battle of Plassey(1757)\n●Buxar(1764): Shah Alam II + Shuja-ud-Daula(Awadh) + Mir Qasim(Bengal) vs British(Hector Munro) — British jeete\n●Plassey(1757): Siraj-ud-Daula vs Clive — alag battle, alag commander\n TRICK — \"3-vs-1 Buxar, 1-vs-1 Plassey\" trick\n💡\nBuxar = 3-party alliance(Emperor+2 Nawabs) vs British — bada coalition. Plassey = sirf 1 Nawab(Siraj) vs Clive —\nchota, single battle. \"Buxar mein Bahut saare log the(3), Plassey mein Plain/simple(1 vs 1)\" — B for Buxar-\nBahut(many), P for Plassey-Plain(simple).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBattle of Buxar(1764) = Shah Alam II+Shuja-ud-Daula+Mir Qasim vs Hector Munro. Battle of Plassey(1757) = Siraj-\nud-Daula vs Clive — dono alag battles, alag commanders, mix mat karo.\n6. Treaty of Allahabad(1765) — Diwani Rights\n●Robert Clive(EIC representative) · EIC ko Bengal+Bihar+Orissa ki Diwani(revenue collection) rights mili\n●Shah Alam II ko English se pension mili\n TRICK — \"Diwani ≠ Direct rule\" trick\n💡\nDiwani = sirf revenue-collection ka adhikaar, DIRECT political control NAHI (shuru mein) — ye British power ka\n\"pehla kadam\" tha, poora control nahi. Yaad rakho: \"paisa collect karne ka haq mila, raaj karne ka nahi — abhi\".\n7. Bahadur Shah II(Zafar) — Aakhri Mughal\n●Revolt of 1857 ke soldiers ka symbolic leader · British ne arrest kiya\n●Death: Rangoon(Myanmar), 1862CE — Delhi/Agra mein NAHI\n TRICK — \"Zafar = Door tak gaya\" trick\n💡\nZafar ko India se bahut door(Rangoon,Myanmar) exile kiya gaya — \"jitna bada raaj, utna door exile\" — ye final irony\nyaad rakho: Mughal Empire jo kabhi poore India pe raaj karta tha, uska aakhri raja Bharat ke bahar hi mara.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nBahadur Shah II(Zafar) ki death Rangoon(Myanmar) mein hui, 1862 CE mein — Delhi ya Agra mein NAHI.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Jajau(1707)-BahadurShahI wins → Nicknames: Bekhbar-Moorkh-Kayar-Rangila(sab weak) → Jizya: Off(Jahandar)-\nOn(Farrukhsiyar)-Off-Permanent(MdShah1720) → Sayyid Brothers=Kingmakers →\nNadirShah(1739,Karnal)=PeacockThrone+Kohinoor(dono) → Buxar(1764,3-vs-1,HectorMunro) vs Plassey(1757,1-\nvs-1,Clive) → Treaty of Allahabad(1765,Clive,Diwani-Bengal/Bihar/Orissa) → BahadurShahII(Zafar)=Rangoon\ndeath(1862)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Jizya finally/permanently abolished = Muhammad Shah (1720), na ki Jahandar Shah.\n2) Buxar(1764,3-party alliance,Hector Munro) ≠ Plassey(1757,Siraj-ud-Daula,Clive).\n3) Nadir Shah ne Peacock Throne AUR Kohinoor DONO liye. Bahadur Shah II ki death Rangoon mein hui.","Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Later Mughal Period","RISE OF MARATHA POWER — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 8 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Shivaji — 2 Coronations, Ek Saal\n●1st Coronation: 6 June 1674 · 2nd Coronation: 24 September 1674 — dono 1674 mein hi\n●Perform ki Gaga Bhatta(Kashi scholar) ne · Guru: Ramdas(Bhakti-Sufi chapter se yaad karo, Samarth Sect founder)\n TRICK — \"2 Coronation, 1 Saal, 3 Mahine Gap\" trick\n💡\nJune aur September — dono 1674 mein, beech mein 3 mahine ka gap(July,Aug beech mein) — ek hi saal ke andar do\nbaar taj pehna, unique fact hai isliye alag se yaad rakho: \"pehli baar June mein, dobara confirm karne September mein\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nShivaji ki coronation DO baar hui — 6 June 1674 aur 24 September 1674, dono SAME YEAR(1674) mein, alag mahino\nmein.\n2. Chauth vs Sardeshmukhi — Fraction Ka Trap\n●Chauth = 1/4(25%) — neighbouring states se, non-aggression ke badle\n●Sardeshmukhi = 1/10(10%) — tribute, Sardeshmukhs dwara\n TRICK — \"Chau=4, Sar-Das=10\" trick\n💡\nChauth mein khud \"Chau\"(=4) hai — 1/4. Sardeshmukhi mein \"Das\"(10) chhupa hua nahi hai literally, par yaad\nrakho: \"Sardeshmukhi = Sar+Desh(pura desh ka daswaan hissa)\" — bada naam wali tax, CHOTI percentage(10%);\nchota naam wali tax(Chauth), BADI percentage(25%) — ulta pattern se yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nChauth = 1/4(25%). Sardeshmukhi = 1/10(10%). Dono alag taxes hain — Chauth non-aggression ke liye, Sardeshmukhi\ntribute ke roop mein.\n3. \"Magna Carta of Marathas\" — Kaunsi Treaty?\n●Magna Carta of Marathas = Delhi Treaty(Balaji Vishwanath + Sayyid Brothers) — Treaty of Purandar NAHI\n TRICK — \"Delhi = Magna Carta\" trick\n💡\nCommon galti: log Treaty of Purandar ko Magna Carta samajh lete hain (kyunki wo bhi famous hai) — GALAT. Yaad\nrakho: \"Delhi mein Balaji Vishwanath ne Sayyid Brothers se badi deal ki, isliye Delhi hi Magna Carta hai\" — Purandar\nShivaji ke time ki hai(purani), Magna Carta baad ki(Peshwa era) hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nMagna Carta of Marathas = Delhi Treaty (Balaji Vishwanath + Sayyid Brothers), NOT Treaty of Purandar.\n4. 2 Treaty of Purandar — Naam Same, Century Alag\n●Purandar 1665: Jai Singh(Mughal) + Shivaji — 23/35 forts diye\n●Purandar 1776: Madhavrao Narayan + British\n TRICK — \"1665=Mughal era, 1776=British era\" trick\n💡\nSame naam, 111 saal ka gap! 1665 = Mughal ke saath(Shivaji ka time), 1776 = British ke saath(Peshwa ka time) —\nbas century dekh ke identify karo: 17th century=Mughal, 18th century=British.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠","2 alag \"Treaty of Purandar\" hain: 1665(Jai Singh+Shivaji, Mughal-Maratha) aur 1776(Madhavrao Narayan+British) —\nnaam same, 111 saal ka gap.\n5. Peshwa — Minister Se Supreme Power Tak\n●Ashtapradhan mein Peshwa = sirf 1 minister(PM jaisa)\n●Balaji Baji Rao ke time Peshwa office HEREDITARY ban gaya → Chhatrapati sirf symbolic reh gaye\n●Baji Rao I = \"Fighting Peshwa\", Maratha Confederacy ke founder\n TRICK — \"Minister → Supreme\" evolution trick\n💡\nPeshwa ka safar: shuru mein 1-of-8 minister → dheere-dheere supreme power → hereditary(Balaji Baji Rao) —\n\"chota role bada ban gaya\", jaise koi employee CEO ban jaaye apni hi company mein.\nBaji Rao I = Founder of Maratha Confederacy — pehla Peshwa jisne ise sach mein empire jaisa banaya, isliye\n\"Fighting\" nickname bhi mila.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nPeshwa Ashtapradhan mein sirf 1 minister tha, par Balaji Baji Rao ke time HEREDITARY ho gaya aur Chhatrapati\npuppet ban gaye.\n6. 4 Maratha Clans — Direct Match\n●Holkar-Indore · Scindia-Gwalior · Gaekwad-Baroda · Bhonsle-Nagpur\n TRICK — \"HSGB\" clan-city trick\n💡\nHolkar-Indore, Scindia-Gwalior, Gaekwad-Baroda, Bhonsle-Nagpur = \"HSGB\" — koi bhi silly sentence bana lo letters\nse, jaise \"Hathi Se Gaya Baazar\".\n7. 3 Anglo-Maratha Wars — Governor-General Match\n●1st(1775-82) = Warren Hastings → Treaty of Salbai\n●2nd(1803-05) = Lord Wellesley → Treaty of Bassein/Deogaon/Surji-Anjangaon\n●3rd(1817-18) = Lord Hastings → Treaty of Poona/Mandasor\n TRICK — \"Warren≠Lord Hastings\" trick\n💡\nWarren Hastings(1st war) aur Lord Hastings(3rd war) — naam mein \"Hastings\" common hai par bilkul ALAG log\nhain, alag wars mein — \"pehla Warren, teesra Lord\" — first-letter se distinguish karo (W for 1st/War-one, L for\nLast/3rd).\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nWarren Hastings(1st Anglo-Maratha War) aur Lord Hastings(3rd Anglo-Maratha War) — do ALAG log hain, naam\nsimilar hone se confuse mat karo.\n8. 3rd Battle of Panipat(1761)\n●14 Jan 1761 → Ahmad Shah Abdali(Afghanistan) ne Marathas(Balaji Baji Rao ki forces) ko haraya\n●Mughals ke against NAHI thi ye battle — Abdali ke against\n TRICK — \"3rd Panipat = Marathas vs Abdali\" trick\n💡\nTeeno Panipat battles alag opponents: 1st(1526)=Babur vs Ibrahim Lodi, 2nd(1556)=Akbar vs Hemu,\n3rd(1761)=Abdali vs MARATHAS(Mughals nahi) — 3rd mein Mughal khud involved nahi tha, Marathas the naye\nplayers.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n3rd Battle of Panipat(1761) = Ahmad Shah Abdali vs MARATHAS (Mughals ke against nahi) — Balaji Baji Rao\nPeshwa the us waqt.\n Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Shivaji: 2 coronations(June+Sept 1674), Guru=Ramdas → Chauth(1/4) vs Sardeshmukhi(1/10) → Magna Carta=Delhi\nTreaty(Balaji Vishwanath+SayyidBros), NOT Purandar → 2 Purandar Treaties(1665-Mughal,1776-British) → Peshwa:\nminister→hereditary(BalajiBajiRao) → BajiRaoI=Fighting Peshwa,founder → 4 clans: HSGB(Holkar-Indore,Scindia-\nGwalior,Gaekwad-Baroda,Bhonsle-Nagpur) → 3 wars: WarrenHastings(1st)-Wellesley(2nd)-LordHastings(3rd) →\n3rdPanipat(1761)=Abdali vs Marathas\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo.\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Magna Carta of Marathas = Delhi Treaty (Balaji Vishwanath+Sayyid Brothers), NOT Treaty of Purandar.\n2) 2 alag Treaty of Purandar: 1665(Mughal-Shivaji) vs 1776(British-Madhavrao).\n3) Warren Hastings(1st war) ≠ Lord Hastings(3rd war) — do alag log.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Rise of Maratha Power","RISE OF THE SIKHS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\nModern History · Chapter 9 (Final Chapter) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain, har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak\njaaye dimaag mein.\n1. Gurmukhi Script — Guru Nanak Ne NAHI\n●Guru Nanak(1st) = Sikhism founder, Sangat+Langar sthapit ki\n●Guru Angad Dev(2nd) = Gurmukhi script shuru ki + Langar regularise\n TRICK — \"Founder≠Script-maker\" trick\n💡\nNanak ne DHARM banaya, Angad ne SCRIPT banayi — founder aur script-creator do alag log hain, jaise koi\ncompany banane wala aur uska logo design karne wala alag ho sakta hai. \"Angad = Anokhi likhawat(Gurmukhi)\" —\ndono \"An\" sound se yaad rakho.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGurmukhi script = Guru Angad Dev(2nd Guru) ne shuru ki — Guru Nanak ne NAHI (unhone sirf Sikhism found ki).\n2. Amritsar City vs Harmandir Sahib — Baap-Beta\n●Amritsar SHEHER = Guru Ram Das(4th Guru) ne basaya\n●Harmandir Sahib(Golden Temple) = Guru Arjan Dev(5th Guru, Ram Das ka beta) ne banaya\n TRICK — \"Baap-Sheher, Beta-Temple\" trick\n💡\nRam Das(baap) ne ZAMEEN(sheher) di, Arjan Dev(beta) ne usi zameen pe MANDIR banaya — ek generation ne\nfoundation rakha, agli generation ne usko poora kiya, jaise ghar-parivaar mein hota hai.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nAmritsar city = Guru Ram Das(4th). Harmandir Sahib/Golden Temple = Guru Arjan Dev(5th, Ram Das ka beta) — city\naur temple ke founders ALAG hain.\n3. 2 Guru Executions — Jahangir vs Aurangzeb\n●Guru Arjan Dev(5th) → JAHANGIR ne execute kiya(1606CE, Khusrau revolt support)\n●Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th) → AURANGZEB ne execute kiya(Islam accept karne se mana kiya)\n TRICK — \"5th-Jahangir, 9th-Aurangzeb\" cross-chapter trick\n💡\nYe EXACT SAME fact Mughal Empire chapter mein bhi tha — 5th Guru(pehle) = Jahangir(pehle raja), 9th\nGuru(baad mein) = Aurangzeb(baad ka raja) — timeline dono jagah match karti hai, cross-verify karo.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGuru Arjan Dev(5th) = Jahangir ne execute kiya. Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th) = Aurangzeb ne execute kiya — number se\nraja match karo, swap mat karo.\n4. Sirf Ek Elected Guru\n●Guru Tegh Bahadur(9th) = SIRF ELECTED Guru — baaki sab hereditary/appointed\n●Guru position hereditary Guru Ram Das(4th) se ban gayi thi\n TRICK — \"9th=akela election\" trick\n💡\n10 mein se sirf 1(9th) elected tha — baaki sab family/appointment se aaye. \"Tegh Bahadur = Thoda Alag(unique\nelection)\" — is uniqueness ko yaad rakho, ye common exam pick hai.","EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nGuru Tegh Bahadur(9th) hi SIRF ELECTED Sikh Guru the — Guru Ram Das(4th) ne position hereditary bana di thi.\n5. Khalsa Panth(1699) vs Dal Khalsa(1748)\n●Khalsa Panth(1699) = Guru Gobind Singh(10th) → religious brotherhood\n●Dal Khalsa(1748) = Kapoor Singh(Jassa Singh Ahluwalia ke under) → military-political confederation, 12 Misls mein\nbata\n TRICK — \"Panth=Dharam, Dal=Fauj\" trick\n💡\nKhalsa PANTH = \"panth\" matlab dharmik samuday (religious group) — Guru Gobind Singh ne banaya. DAL Khalsa\n= \"dal\" matlab sena/army (Dal-Sena jaisa sound) — baad mein banaya political-military confederation — naam mein hi\n\"religious vs military\" ka farak chhupa hai.\n49 saal ka gap(1699→1748) — ek generation baad, dharmik samuday se military confederation tak ka safar.\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nKhalsa Panth(1699,Guru Gobind Singh)=religious brotherhood. Dal Khalsa(1748,Kapoor Singh)=military-political\nconfederation, 12 Misls mein bata — dono alag cheezein.\n6. 2 \"Treaty of Amritsar\" — Year Se Pehchano\n●1809 CE = Ranjit Singh + Charles Metcalfe → Sutlej boundary fix, British supremacy(south of Sutlej) accept ki\n●1849 CE(2nd Anglo-Sikh War end) = British ne Kohinoor liya, Duleep Singh pensioner ban gaye\n TRICK — \"1809=Boundary, 1849=Kohinoor\" trick\n💡\n40 saal ka gap: 1809 = Ranjit Singh KHUD zinda tha, boundary-deal(peaceful). 1849 = Ranjit Singh ki maut ke\nbaad(1839), empire kamzor, Kohinoor bhi gaya — \"pehle deal, baad mein sab kuch gaya\".\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\nTreaty of Amritsar(1809)=Ranjit Singh+Metcalfe, Sutlej boundary. Treaty of Amritsar(1849, alag context)=2nd Anglo-\nSikh War end, Kohinoor liya — year se identify karo.\n7. 2 Anglo-Sikh Wars — Governor-General Match\n●1st(1845-46) = Lord Hardinge → Treaty of Lahore(1846)\n●2nd(1848-49) = Lord Dalhousie → Kohinoor liya, Duleep Singh pension\n TRICK — \"Hardinge-Lahore, Dalhousie-Kohinoor\" trick\n💡\nHardinge(1st) → Lahore treaty. Dalhousie(2nd) → Kohinoor — dono pairs alphabetically bhi roughly match: H-before-\nD(1st-before-2nd), L-before-K nahi but bas number-order se yaad rakho: 1st Governor-General ne treaty ki, 2nd wale ne\ndiamond liya.\n8. Panj Kakar (5 K's) & Ranjit Singh\n●5 K's: Kesh · Kangha · Kara · Kachha · Kirpan\n●Ranjit Singh: Sukerchakia Misl · pita Maha Singh · 12 saal mein Misl chief bane · Lahore(1799,political capital) →\nAmritsar(1802,cultural capital)\n TRICK — \"5K + Ranjit's 2 capitals\" trick\n💡\n5 K's sab \"K\" se shuru hote hain — bas ginti yaad rakho: 5 K's. Lahore=Political(pehle liya,1799),\nAmritsar=Cultural(baad mein,1802) — political power pehle, cultural/religious center baad mein aaya.","Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n🔗\n 1-Line Revision Chain\n🔗\n\"Nanak(founder)→Angad(Gurmukhi)→AmarDas→RamDas(Amritsar city,hereditary)→ArjanDev(Harmandir\nSahib,Jahangir executed) → Hargobind(AkalTakht)→HarRai→Harkrishan(youngest)→TeghBahadur(ONLY\nelected,Aurangzeb executed)→GobindSingh(KhalsaPanth1699,5K's,last Guru) → BandaBahadur(1st political\nleader,Farrukhsiyar executed) → DalKhalsa(1748,KapoorSingh) → RanjitSingh(Sukerchakia,Lahore+Amritsar) →\nTreatyofAmritsar1809(Metcalfe,Sutlej) → 2 Anglo-Sikh Wars: Hardinge(1st,Lahore treaty)-Dalhousie(2nd,Kohinoor)\"\nRoz ek baar seedha bol ke revise karo — ye Medieval History set ka LAST chapter hai!\n Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n⚠\n EXAM TRAP\n⚠\n1) Gurmukhi = Guru Angad Dev(2nd), NOT Guru Nanak.\n2) Amritsar city=Guru Ram Das(4th). Harmandir Sahib=Guru Arjan Dev(5th) — do alag Gurus.\n3) Khalsa Panth(1699,Guru Gobind Singh)≠Dal Khalsa(1748,Kapoor Singh) — dharmik vs military-political.\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Ancient History Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Rise of the Sikhs (Final Chapter)"];
